target: internal/report/post.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheBranchesNothingReached/a_binary_of_the_wrong_format'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    "could not start" was decided by enumerating sentinels — ErrNotFound, ErrNotExist, ErrPermission — and that list misses the binary that EXISTS, is executable, and is the wrong format. Measured: a chmod +x text file gives a *fs.PathError ("exec format error") matching none of the three and not an *exec.ExitError either, so it fell through to the default, left Runnable true, and reported "gh ran and failed — Step 0c can flush it once gh works" for a gh that never ran. That is the wrong remedy twice: it tells the operator to wait for GitHub when the fix is to reinstall. Wait can only ever report an ExitError, so the INVERSE test is the complete one and an enumeration never can be.
--- old
	case !errors.As(err, new(*exec.ExitError)):
--- new
	case errors.Is(err, exec.ErrNotFound), errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist), errors.Is(err, os.ErrPermission):
